# TypeScript Conventions

- Use strict TypeScript. Avoid `any`; prefer `unknown` with type guards or well-defined types.
- Keep components small and focused; extract reusable logic into custom hooks in `hooks/`.
- Use Tailwind CSS for layout and styling; avoid inline styles except for dynamic values derived from runtime data.
- Prefer server-side token handling in Next.js API routes; never expose Spotify tokens to the browser.
- Name components in PascalCase and hooks/utilities in camelCase.
- Add explicit return types for public library functions and API route handlers when possible.
